  "18c0a3bf-fa55-443d-80e8-769c4fd13ec0"],
 "\n\nThe notation for the Birkhoff diamond coloring requires some \
explanation.  The left and right side of each spoke is given a number from 1 \
to 12.  In addition, we label each edge of a blowup 3-cycle with a number, \
following a counterclockwise orientation (as a convention).  The conventions \
are the same as what we used to for the arcs in our colored caps.  Given \
arc[c,A[a1,...,an]], c represents the color and A[a1,..,an] represents the \
arc.  The difference is that instead of using two numbers to indicate the \
arc, we use multiple numbers to represent a circle.  The list of numbers in \
each arc represents a circle containing each of these numbered arcs.  The \
list is given in numerical order, not in the order they appear as you follow \
the path.  For example, the red loop, arc[1,A[4,9,16,21,28,38,40]] represents \
the following circle:\n",
